BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T143000
UID:69b45639a2492930199a12ed@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Share your love of reading at our Wednesday and Thursday Book 
 Clubs! We discuss new books and old favourites in a friendly\, welcoming s
 etting. Ask staff for more details.\nApr 8 - The Women by Kristin Hannah\n
 May 13 - The Kiss Quotient by Helen Hoang\nJune 10 - James by Percival E
 verett\nJuly 8 - My Brilliant Friend by Elena Ferrante\nAug 12 - The Sound
  of Gravel by Ruth Wariner\nSept 9 - A House Without Windows by Nadia Hash
 imi\nOct 14 - Tomorrow and Tomorrow and Tomorrow by Gabrielle Zevin\nNov 1
 1 - The Betrayal of Anne Frank by Rosemary Sullivan\nDec 9 - How to Solve 
 Your Own Murder by Kristen Perrin
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b45639a2492930199a12ed
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Web Design for Entrepreneurs (Newcomer Stream)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T193000
UID:69d95a8ec1cf6f9a75847e26@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this\n8-week course\n\, learn how to build a strong web pre
 sence for your business in Toronto\, whether you’re launching something 
 new or already running one. Explore how to create a website using WordPres
 s and understand why it remains a powerful tool\, even in the age of AI we
 bsite builders. While AI can help you get started quickly\, WordPress giv
 es you full control over your content\, updates\, and long-term growth. By
  the end\, you’ll feel more confident managing your own website\, saving
  costs while strengthening your marketing at the same time.\nParticipants 
 should plan to attend all 8 of the following d\nates:\nMay 6\, May 13\,\n
 May 20\nJune 3\, June 17\, June 24\nJuly 8\, July 15\nRegistration is requ
 ired for the full series\n. This program is hosted by the Business\, Scien
 ce and Technology department. Please visit the 4th floor service desk or c
 all (416) 395-5613 for more information.\nThis program is part of the\n"Bu
 ilding your own Website for Small Business" Program Series (Newcomer strea
 m)\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, e-Learning Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d95a8ec1cf6f9a75847e26
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
