BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T153000
UID:69d8176a1e64afd01e681c25@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Weston Branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety o
 f trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry team to explore the natur
 al world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different s
 pecies and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\nChil
 dren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nThe tour will st
 art and end at the Weston Branch and will be guided by the City of Toronto
  Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the ro
 ute. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. g
 loves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This progra
 m takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, re
 gistrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nThis program is part o
 f TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toro
 nto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Weston\, Youth Hub Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d8176a1e64afd01e681c25
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Night Sparrow: Celebrating Unsung Jewish Women Erased From His
 tory
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260511T153000
UID:69ab65c74a9fd98b7f82a5a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The first Jewish female snipers in history fought against the 
 'fascist Nazis' in WWII\, yet their astonishing stories are visually unkno
 wn. Forbidden to speak about their achievements after the war\, these wome
 n were erased by the country they fought to protect.\nDiscover how these i
 ndomitable women changed history in this presentation by author Shelly San
 ders\, whose novel\nThe Night Sparrow\nwas inspired by their recently tran
 slated diaries\, photos\, and frontline stories.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room B on the third floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab65c74a9fd98b7f82a5a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Movie Screening: Marmalade
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T200000
UID:69961fbcb0595799c09dc5bf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month's feature:\nMarmalade\nEnjoy a night at the movies!
  Join us for a free movie on the big screen in our accessible theatre.\nDe
 scription: MARMALADE is an edge-of-the-seat crime-tinged romance tale. Re
 cently incarcerated Baron struck up a friendship with cellmate Otis\, a ma
 n with a well-versed history of prison breaks. As the pair hatch an escape
  plan together\, Baron recalls the story of how he met Marmalade\, the lov
 e of his life\, and their "Bonnie and Clyde" style scheme to rob a bank in
  order to care for his sick mother and give the couple the life they have 
 always dreamed of.\nThis film is rated 14A. 99 minutes. Start time is 6:00
  pm. Drop in. All are welcome!
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre (downstairs)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69961fbcb0595799c09dc5bf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
